      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## InfluxDB Internals \u2014 engine & operational self-monitoring\n\nInfluxDB's own `/metrics` (Prometheus) scraped by **Telegraf** (`inputs.prometheus`, 60s)\ninto the `system` bucket \u2014 one measurement per metric. Counters are shown as **per-second\nrates** (`derivative`); gauges as-is.\n\n| Section | Metric |\n|---|---|\n| Write throughput / errors / dropped | `storage_writer_ok_points` / `_err_points` / `_dropped_points` (`sum`) |\n| Query rate + controller state | `qc_requests_total`, `qc_*_active` |\n| HTTP API + I/O | `http_api_requests_total`, `http_*_bytes` |\n| Meta store | `boltdb_reads_total` / `boltdb_writes_total` |\n| Inventory + uptime | `influxdb_*_total`, `influxdb_uptime_seconds` |\n\n**Hybrid with [InfluxDB Buckets](/d/influxdb-buckets):** this board owns the *engine/operational*\ninternals; the `bucket-stats` collector owns *named per-bucket storage + throughput*, which\n`/metrics` can't label by name or derive. The scrape `namedrop`s the cardinality bombs\n(`*_duration_seconds` histograms, per-shard `storage_*`, Go/promhttp/process runtime) \u2192 ~50\nbounded series. Source: `telegraf/telegraf.conf`.\n"
      }
    }
